       ("Replying to positive reviews", "<p>Thank the customer by name if they used one, mention something specific about their visit, and keep it brief. Example: <em>Thanks, Maria. Glad the new water heater is working well, and thanks for the kind words about Luis.</em></p>"),
       ("Replying to negative reviews", "<p>Google notes that negative reviews are not necessarily a sign of poor business practice and can help you understand expectations. Acknowledge the problem, apologize where appropriate, explain briefly without arguing, and offer a way to resolve it offline. Example: <em>We are sorry the appointment ran late, James. That is not the experience we want. Please call our office manager at the number on our profile so we can make it right.</em></p>"),
       ("When customers update reviews", "<p>Google says the reviewer is notified when you reply, and customers can still change their review afterward; the date then updates. A constructive reply sometimes leads to an improved review.</p>"),
